                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything that flattens."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4af57f47-d34a-35cb-b225-8bfe21516b0d",
                                        "entry_id": "50460c07-2fb5-3c1a-8e44-1716deccff8b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A trade whose terms are based on the assumption that the rate of return will decrease."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56896add-b9f6-4624-9f3a-7a7eab51f3ea",
                                                "sense_id": "4af57f47-d34a-35cb-b225-8bfe21516b0d",
                                                "text": "Provided that the curve doesn't ever flatten too much and the option remains out-of-the-money, then we will put on flatteners when the curve steepens and put on steepeners when the curve flattens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0bb1b36-ab29-419a-a43b-c0db779e93fd",
                                                "sense_id": "4af57f47-d34a-35cb-b225-8bfe21516b0d",
                                                "text": "For example, if a trader thought that 2's 10's would trade lower than 185, he or she would put on a flattener."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
